@@ replace
This is also the fallback path for HubSpot, Pipedrive and Attio when no connector or key is available.
@@ with
This is also the fallback path for HubSpot, Pipedrive and Attio when no connector is available. This edition takes a file of about 200 rows or fewer; a larger file needs Tessary GTM Pro (`${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/reference/upgrade.md`, trigger 2).
@@ replace
No connector or key. The file is read by `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/lib/csv_import.py`:

```
python3 -I -B ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/lib/csv_import.py fields
python3 -I -B ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/lib/csv_import.py suggest <file.csv> [--out mapping.json]
python3 -I -B ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/lib/csv_import.py plan <file.csv> --mapping mapping.json [--existing keys.json] [--allow-keyless]
    [--owner-emails a@x.com,b@x.com] [--own-domains x.com] [--include-owner] [--out plan.json]
python3 -I -B ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/lib/csv_import.py self-test
```

Without `--owner-emails` and `--own-domains`, `plan` reads `owner.emails` and `owner.own_domains` from the config. `self-test` checks the planner against a built-in sample file and exits 0 when every check passes.

The script never writes to Notion and never reaches the network. It detects the delimiter (comma, semicolon, tab, pipe) and strips a UTF-8 byte order mark.
@@ with
No connector or key. Read the file with the Read tool, and map and plan it yourself (`${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/skills/import/references/apply.md`, Flatten and Plan by hand). The delimiter can be a comma, semicolon, tab or pipe; ignore a UTF-8 byte order mark at the start.
@@ replace
2. `csv_import.py suggest <file>` exits 0 and shows at least one column mapped to `email` or `linkedin`. If none is, ask which columns hold the email and the LinkedIn URL. Without either, every row is skipped (no stable key) unless the user agrees to `--allow-keyless` and the file has a record id column.
3. Say the row count and the column list back to the user.
@@ with
2. At least one column holds an email or a LinkedIn URL. If none does, ask which columns hold the email and the LinkedIn URL. Without either, every row is skipped (no stable key) unless the user agrees to keyless rows and the file has a record id column.
3. Say the row count and the column list back to the user. Count the data rows before you create the run folder or copy the file. More than about 200: stop with the upgrade message (`${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/reference/upgrade.md`, trigger 2).
@@ replace
1. `suggest` the mapping. Show columns, three sample rows and the guess.
@@ with
1. Propose the mapping (`${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/skills/import/SKILL.md`, step 4). Show columns, three sample rows and the proposal.
@@ replace
 Map the record id column, if any, to `extra` and also add a `Source ID` column as described in `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/skills/import/references/apply.md`, Flatten. The `Source ID` column maps to `source_id`.
@@ with
 Map the record id column, if any, to `source_id` as described in `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/skills/import/references/apply.md`, Flatten.
